//
// SUMMARY
// -------
// The state==4 (LINK_IDLE) -> state==5 (LINK_DATA) transition fires ONLY on
// `a2l_fc_replay.link.valid && ~fe_rx_is_full` (FC.scala:523, _GEN_60 at line
// 430 of the local override). This is a *producer-side* gate: the FCSM only
// moves to LINK_DATA when ITS OWN application has FC data to send.
//
// In the pair-sim Bug A repro and on HW (build #3), the slave's app does NOT
// drive a2l traffic. As a result the slave FCSM rests at state 4 forever, even
// though the master is sending data packets. The RX framer combinational
// outputs (l2a_fc_replay_app_valid at line 719) DO sample regardless of
// state, but the FCSM staying at 4 keeps the SOP/data_id/word_count regs
// quiescent on the slave's TX side; the upstream Wlink expects the FCSM to be
// in state 5 to ack with credit. So practically the link is wedged.
//
// FIX (L8 consumer-side analogue of L7):
//   1. Latch a sticky observation that the *peer is sending data* — proxy:
//        socl_l8_peer_data_seen <= pkt_is_data_pkt | socl_l8_peer_data_seen
//      (io_rx_clk-domain register; cleared only on `reset` like cr/crack
//      sticky bits in the L6 fix at lines 866-879).
//   2. Synchronize that sticky into io_tx_clk via a 2-flop demet
//      (use an inline pair of regs identical in style to
//      cr_pkt_seen_tx_demet).
//   3. Compute a bring-up forgive gate analogous to L7:
//        wire socl_l8_consumer_data_ready =
//             cr_pkt_seen_tx_demet_io_out
//           & crack_pkt_seen_tx_demet_io_out
//           & socl_l8_peer_data_seen_tx_demet_io_out
//           & ~send_nack_req
//           & ~socl_l8_reached_link_data;
//   4. Override _GEN_60 (the state==4 next-state expression) so that the
//      forgive gate forces 3'h5:
//        wire [2:0] _GEN_60 = socl_l8_consumer_data_ready ? 3'h5
//                            : (a2l_fc_replay_link_valid & ~fe_rx_is_full)
//                              ? 3'h5 : state;
//   5. Mirror the L7 "reached_link_data" sticky for L8 so the gate disarms
//      permanently once state 5 has been seen once:
//        reg socl_l8_reached_link_data;
//        always @(posedge io_tx_clk or posedge io_tx_reset)
//          if (io_tx_reset) socl_l8_reached_link_data <= 0;
//          else if (state == 3'h5) socl_l8_reached_link_data <= 1'b1;
//
// SAFETY
// ------
//   * Once state 5 is observed even once, the L8 gate is permanently disarmed
//     until reset — steady-state behaviour matches upstream.
//   * The L8 gate is GATED on cr/crack having been observed AND on having
//     seen a real data packet from the peer — so it cannot fire before the
//     link is structurally healthy.
//   * The natural upstream path (a2l_fc_replay_link_valid && ~fe_rx_is_full)
//     still fires when the local app has data. L8 is purely an *additional*
//     trigger.
//   * Once in state 5, the upstream `nstate := LINK_IDLE` fall-back (Chisel
//     line 565-566) returns the FSM to state 4 when there's no TX work.  But
//     because socl_l8_reached_link_data is now sticky, the L8 gate will not
//     re-fire — so the FSM will only re-enter state 5 via the natural a2l
//     path, exactly like upstream. This avoids a state 4 <-> 5 thrash.
//   * L8 does NOT modify the state==1 / state==2 / state==3 branches. The L6
//     producer-side fix on state==1 is untouched. The L7 send_nack_req clear
//     remains valid in every state.
//
// RISKS
// -----
//   * If the data packet decoder produces false positives during bringup
//     (e.g. mid-byte mis-align decoding a CR as data), socl_l8_peer_data_seen
//     could latch spuriously. Mitigation: we gate L8 on cr/crack having
//     already been observed.  If desired, AND-in
//     `~socl_l7_bringup_forgive` to delay L8 until L7 has retired.
//   * If both peers reach state 4 at exactly the same cycle, both could fire
//     L8 to state 5 simultaneously — but that is also the steady-state
//     desired outcome. No deadlock.
//   * On WlinkGenericFCSM_4.v (sister generated module, different state
//     encoding): NOT patched here. If FCSM_4 is also used in the pair link
//     RTL, audit independently before claiming the fix is complete.
//
// =============================================================================
// PROPOSED UNIFIED DIFF (git-apply against src/rtl/local_overrides/
// WlinkGenericFCSM_6.v at current HEAD). Apply manually after review.
// =============================================================================

--- a/src/rtl/local_overrides/WlinkGenericFCSM_6.v
+++ b/src/rtl/local_overrides/WlinkGenericFCSM_6.v
@@ -296,6 +296,11 @@
   reg [7:0] fe_rx_credit_max; // @[FC.scala 183:107]
   reg  cr_pkt_seen_rx; // @[FC.scala 186:107]
